From 884c9418170eb8b4c443a4ab38ef3cc14b91f5e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christian F.K. Schaller" <christian.schaller@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:14:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] scanner: Add the dialog for the scanner portal

This commit implements org.freedesktop.impl.portal.Scanner, whose one
method, SelectScanners, shows a dialog that lists the scanners the
frontend found and returns the ids of the ones the user chose. It is
modelled on the USB dialog: the backend only asks for consent, and the
frontend does the work of talking to the scanner.

The dialog is a libadwaita window with a list of rows, one per scanner,
each showing the name, how it is connected and what it can scan (film,
flatbed, feeder). It honours the modal, multiple, accept_label and title
options of the frontend call. With multiple unset the rows are radio
buttons, and the first scanner that is available is chosen already, so
that one click is enough when there is one scanner. Scanners that are
not available are shown and cannot be chosen. The heading names the
application, which the portal supplies, and the application's own title
is shown under it as secondary text. With no scanners it shows an empty
state. The window is sized to the list.

Cancel, Escape and closing the window answer with the cancelled
response, and Request.Close destroys the dialog without an answer,
because the frontend answers a closed request itself.

The interface XML is copied into data/ because an installed
xdg-desktop-portal does not carry the Scanner interface yet. The copy
and the special case in src/meson.build go away when it does.

Tested by calling SelectScanners on a private bus with made-up scanners:
select, Escape, the Cancel button and Request.Close, and the layout on a
Wayland session. Not tested with a real frontend or a parent window.
